    <string name="explain_pslc_title">Wear Level A: pSLC</string>
    <string name="explain_pslc_desc">Slot A reports wear from cells operating in pseudo-SLC mode. Controllers use this high-speed cache for writes and metadata. It has the highest endurance and usually wears much slower than the main storage array.</string>
    <string name="explain_tlc_mlc_title">Wear Level B: TLC / MLC</string>
    <string name="explain_tlc_mlc_desc">Slot B reports wear from the main user storage array. This is the primary indicator of the physical lifespan of your apps, photos, media, and system partitions.</string>
    <string name="explain_preeol_title">Pre-EOL: Spare Blocks Health</string>
    <string name="explain_preeol_desc">Pre-End of Life reports how many reserved spare blocks have been consumed. Normal (0x01) is under 80 percent, Warning (0x02) is about 80 percent, and Urgent (0x03) is over 90 percent.</string>

